From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:09:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] network: skip SO_PEERCRED unix socket peer pid on QNX

net_address_unix_socket_peer_pid_raw() reads the peer process id of a unix
socket with getsockopt(SO_PEERCRED) and struct ucred. QNX's <sys/socket.h>
defines no SO_PEERCRED option, so the peer credentials cannot be read this
way and the code does not compile.

Treat QNX like macOS and FreeBSD: the code that needs struct ucred and
SO_PEERCRED is compiled out and the function reports that no peer pid is
available.

Signed-off-by: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/flb_network.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/flb_network.c b/src/flb_network.c
index 6a65a07..3d7eacf 100644
--- a/src/flb_network.c
+++ b/src/flb_network.c
@@ -2150,7 +2150,7 @@ static int net_address_unix_socket_peer_pid_raw(flb_sockfd_t fd,
                                                 int output_buffer_size,
                                                 size_t *output_data_size)
 {
-#if !defined(FLB_SYSTEM_MACOS) && !defined(FLB_SYSTEM_FREEBSD)
+#if !defined(FLB_SYSTEM_MACOS) && !defined(FLB_SYSTEM_FREEBSD) && !defined(FLB_SYSTEM_QNX)
     unsigned int peer_credentials_size;
     struct ucred peer_credentials;
 #endif
@@ -2168,7 +2168,7 @@ static int net_address_unix_socket_peer_pid_raw(flb_sockfd_t fd,
         return -1;
     }
 
-#if !defined(FLB_SYSTEM_MACOS) && !defined(FLB_SYSTEM_FREEBSD)
+#if !defined(FLB_SYSTEM_MACOS) && !defined(FLB_SYSTEM_FREEBSD) && !defined(FLB_SYSTEM_QNX)
     peer_credentials_size = sizeof(struct ucred);
 
     result = getsockopt(fd,
